    "narrative": "The standout play for Ghost Ride the WHIP today is undeniably **Corbin Carroll**, boasting a team-high score of 85.94 against Paredes. His profile benefits from a favorable SP_xERA of 4.94, and the synergy of hitting third in the order while maintaining a robust platoon advantage against a righty sets the stage for a ceiling performance. Joining him in the elite tier are **Gabriel Moreno** (69.96) and **Brice Turang** (68.34). **Brice Turang** is particularly compelling; while the base projection is modest, his score is bolstered by a +4% efficiency boost stemming from the opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, a crucial metric given our mandate to prioritize stolen bases in this 5x5 format. Meanwhile, **James Wood** (65.61) provides a strong floor at the top of the order, with his elite 0.404 xwOBA offsetting the -6% park factor.\n\nWe have opted to bench **Max Muncy** (45.66), who was the most difficult exclusion from the starting lineup. **Max Muncy** carries an attractive park factor against Detmers, but the sub-40 ceiling of **Cole Young** and the sheer depth of our infield forced him into a supporting role today; the optimizer favored the higher overall efficiency of **Austin Riley** (64.84) against a vulnerable Gasser. We remain wary of **Tyler Soderstrom** and **Jose Caballero**, both of whom are facing difficult left-handed or elite-skill right-handed opposition that has depressed their scores toward the marginal threshold. We are holding tight on **Trevor Story** and **Mickey Moniak** as they remain on the IL, but the offensive output today rests squarely on **Corbin Carroll** and **James Wood** to generate the necessary runs and speed to stay competitive in the standings.",
